+From c50b969d2734ef0b4526bda780a7394626ae6c64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:34:59 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] [settings] Add Dolby Vision defaults to Player / Videos
+
+The Dolby Vision options could only be set from the video settings
+dialog during playback, so they could not be found or set from Kodi's
+settings. Add a Dolby Vision group to Player / Videos with the
+enhancement layer, the infoframe and, at the Expert level, the
+enhancement layer upscale, the chroma MMR and the filters. Every video
+starts with them, and "Set as default for all media" in the video
+settings dialog stores its choices there.
+
+The video database does not store the Dolby Vision options, so a file
+with stored video settings now takes them, and the Dolby Vision output
+toggle, from the defaults rather than from CVideoSettings' own.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
